From: Douglas Teles <dga.teles@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817-battery: report charging from an
 external charger

The R36S and its clones charge the battery with a separate charger IC:
the charge LED lights and the gauge measures 0.5 to 0.65 A flowing into
the pack, but VBUS never reaches the RK817, so PLUG_IN_STS stays clear,
the plug-in interrupt never fires and the RK817 charger reports
CHRG_OFF. The battery status then reads "Not charging" while the pack
is charging, and the UI never shows it.

When the RK817 charger is off and unplugged but the averaged gauge
current is at least 10 mA into the pack, report Charging. The current
tapers well below 100 mA in the constant-voltage phase, while running
on battery the gauge always reads a clearly negative current.

diff --color -ru a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -486,6 +486,9 @@
 	rk817_bat_calib_cap(charger);
 }
 
+/* Net charge current that means an external charger is feeding the pack. */
+#define RK817_EXT_CHRG_MIN_UA	10000
+
 static int rk817_bat_get_prop(struct power_supply *ps,
 		enum power_supply_property prop,
 		union power_supply_propval *val)
@@ -503,7 +506,17 @@
 		}
 		switch (charger->charge_status) {
 		case CHRG_OFF:
-			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
+			/*
+			 * Some boards (R36S and clones) charge the pack with a
+			 * separate charger IC and never route VBUS to the
+			 * RK817, so its charger stays off while the gauge sees
+			 * the pack taking current.
+			 */
+			if (!charger->plugged_in &&
+			    charger->cur_avg_ua >= RK817_EXT_CHRG_MIN_UA)
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+			else
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 			break;
 		/*
 		 * Dead charge is documented, but not explained. I never
